### Takedown

If you hold rights to any bundled content and want it removed, open an issue in this
repository (or contact the maintainer through the repository's listed contact). The
relevant directory or migration range will be removed promptly. The application is
designed so that content can be removed without touching code:

- question bank → delete the `drizzle/*_data_*.sql` migrations
- textbook → delete `seed/textbook_seed.sql.gz` and `textbooks/`
- figures → delete `public/emidici-assets/`

With the content removed the app still builds and runs; it simply has no questions
to serve until you supply your own.

